id: k8s.service.clusterip
kind: kubernetes
title: ClusterIP service
aliases: cluster ip, internal service
tags: networking, service
questions:
  - what happens when you create a ClusterIP service?
invariant: A virtual IP reachable only from inside the cluster, load-balanced across ready endpoints.
answer_30s: ClusterIP is the default Service type: a cluster-internal virtual IP plus DNS name mapping to the ready Pods.
when_to_use:
  - service-to-service traffic inside the cluster
avoid_when:
  - you need external access (Ingress or LoadBalancer)
commands:
  - kubectl get svc api -o yaml => confirm type, clusterIP and selector
failure_modes:
  - expecting a ClusterIP to be reachable from your laptop (use port-forward)
related:
  - k8s.service
  - k8s.port-forward
sources:
  - https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/services-networking/service/#publishing-services-service-types
